@@ -1,5 +1,17 @@
 # Changelog
 
+## 1.6.0
+
+- Ticket assignment. `PUT /tickets/:id/assignee` with `{"assignee": "<agent>"}` assigns an open or in-progress ticket to
+  an agent (a name of at most 64 characters) and `{"assignee": null}` unassigns it; the agent is notified. Every ticket
+  shows its `assignee`, null when unassigned (while `DUE_TIMES` is off a ticket nobody is assigned to does not show the
+  field yet, so the API stays as it was before 1.5.0 until that setting is on).
+- `GET /tickets?assignee=<agent>` lists an agent's tickets; an empty `assignee=` lists the unassigned ones.
+- Fix: filters now combine as documented. A ticket is listed only when it matches every filter given; before, it was listed
+  when it matched any one of them.
+- The command line shows each ticket's assignee: an ASSIGNEE column in `list`, a fifth column in `list --raw` (after
+  the title, so the report's columns keep their positions), and `--assignee` to filter.
+
 ## 1.5.0
 
 - Due times ([decision 9](docs/decisions/0009-due-times.md)). Every ticket gets a due time, `due`: the time it was created
